IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fta-types`

-- Fair Trading Act 1986 — GOAL 1: CONDUCT.
--
--   "Does this conduct contravene the provision engaged; does s 15 (news
--    media), s 12A(3) or s 12D take it outside the Act; may a party to a
--    contract seek an order despite a contracting-out clause; and the rules
--    on vendor bids, unsolicited goods and specified trade contracts."
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1986_121.txt — ss 2-5D,
-- Part 1.

§ `Goal 1 — conduct`

§§ `Which provisions need conduct "in trade"`

-- Sections 7, 9, 10, 11, 12A, 13, 14(1), 16, 19(1), 21A(2) ("If the sender
-- is in trade"), 21C, 28B (a vendor in trade), 32 ("has in trade supplied
-- goods"; (5) "shall not, in trade, supply"), 36WB and 36WC are limited to
-- conduct "in trade"; the others apply to any person. s 19(2) says "Any
-- person who has advertised", without "in trade" (changed after the
-- independent pass).
@ref ss 7, 9-14, 16, 19, 21C, 28B, 36WB, 36WC
GIVEN p IS A Prohibition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision applies only in trade` p IF
       p EQUALS `s 7 unconscionable conduct in trade`
    OR p EQUALS `s 9 misleading or deceptive conduct in trade`
    OR p EQUALS `s 10 conduct liable to mislead the public about goods`
    OR p EQUALS `s 11 conduct liable to mislead the public about services`
    OR p EQUALS `s 12A an unsubstantiated representation in trade`
    OR p EQUALS `s 13 a false or misleading representation about goods or services`
    OR p EQUALS `s 14(1) a false or misleading representation about land`
    OR p EQUALS `s 16 forging or falsely applying a trade mark`
    OR p EQUALS `s 19 bait advertising`
    OR p EQUALS `s 21A(2) a trader sending unsolicited goods without telling the recipient their rights`
    OR p EQUALS `s 21C asserting a right to payment for unsolicited goods or services`
    OR p EQUALS `s 32 a compulsory recall notice`
    OR p EQUALS `s 28B disclosing trader status online`
    OR p EQUALS `s 36WB a gift card expiring in less than 3 years`
    OR p EQUALS `s 36WC a gift card without a prominent expiry`

-- s 15 applies to "sections 9 to 14".
@ref s 15
GIVEN p IS A Prohibition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is one of sections 9 to 14` p IF
       p EQUALS `s 9 misleading or deceptive conduct in trade`
    OR p EQUALS `s 10 conduct liable to mislead the public about goods`
    OR p EQUALS `s 11 conduct liable to mislead the public about services`
    OR p EQUALS `s 12 misleading conduct about employment`
    OR p EQUALS `s 12A an unsubstantiated representation in trade`
    OR p EQUALS `s 13 a false or misleading representation about goods or services`
    OR p EQUALS `s 14(1) a false or misleading representation about land`
    OR p EQUALS `s 14(2) force, harassment or coercion about land`

-- s 15 "(1) Nothing in sections 9 to 14 applies to the publication of any
-- information or matter in a newspaper by the publisher of that newspaper,
-- not being— (a) the publication of an advertisement; or (b) the publication
-- of any information or matter relating to the supply ... by— (i) that
-- publisher ...; or (ii) any person who is a party to any contract,
-- arrangement, or understanding with that publisher relating to the content
-- ..." (2) the same for broadcasting.
@ref s 15
GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `News media facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the news media exception applies to` m IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST n THEN
            n's `published in a newspaper or broadcast by the publisher or broadcaster`
        AND NOT n's `an advertisement`
        AND NOT n's `about the publisher's or broadcaster's own supply, or a party's under an arrangement with it`

-- The contravention. s 4(1) "this Act shall bind the Crown in so far as the
-- Crown engages in trade". s 12A(3) "This section does not apply to a
-- representation that a reasonable person would not expect to be
-- substantiated." s 12D: a person who complies with another enactment that
-- sets the grounds for representations in their trade.
@ref ss 4, 7-36ZF, 12A(3), 12D, 15
@export Whether conduct contravenes the provision engaged under the Fair Trading Act 1986 (NZ): the conduct has the quality the provision describes, is in trade where the provision requires it, is not the Crown acting otherwise than in trade (s 4), is not news media publication outside advertising and the publisher's own supply (s 15, for ss 9-14), and, for an unsubstantiated representation, is not one a reasonable person would not expect to be substantiated or one made in compliance with another enactment (ss 12A(3), 12D). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct case`  @desc The provision engaged, whether the conduct has the quality it describes, whether in trade, the kind of person and whether the Crown, any news media facts, and the s 12A(3) and s 12D facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct contravenes the provision` c IF
        c's `the conduct has the quality the provision describes`
    AND (c's `in trade` OR NOT `the provision applies only in trade` (c's `provision engaged`))
    AND (c's `in trade` OR NOT c's `the person is the Crown`)
    AND NOT (`is one of sections 9 to 14` (c's `provision engaged`) AND `the news media exception applies to` (c's `news media`))
    AND NOT (    c's `provision engaged` EQUALS `s 12A an unsubstantiated representation in trade`
             AND (c's `a reasonable person would not expect substantiation` OR c's `complied with another enactment setting the grounds`))

§§ `Contracting out (ss 5C, 5D)`

-- s 5D(3) "(a) the agreement is in writing; and (b) the goods, services, or
-- interest in land are both supplied and acquired in trade; and (c) all
-- parties to the agreement— (i) are in trade; and (ii) agree to contract out
-- of section 9, 12A, 13, or 14(1); and (d) it is fair and reasonable that
-- the parties are bound".
@ref s 5D(3)
GIVEN k IS A `Contracting out clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the clause validly contracts out under s 5D` k IF
        k's `the agreement is in writing`
    AND k's `supplied and acquired in trade`
    AND k's `all parties are in trade`
    AND k's `all parties agree to contract out`
    AND k's `it is fair and reasonable that the parties are bound`

-- s 5D(1)(b) "no proceedings may be brought by any party to the agreement for
-- an order under section 43 in relation to such a contravention of section
-- 9, 12A, 13, or 14(1)". s 12C "only the Commission may commence
-- proceedings, apply for an order, or apply for an injunction in relation to
-- a contravention of section 12A."
@ref ss 5C, 5D, 12C, 43
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a party may apply for an order under s 43` c IF
        NOT c's `provision engaged` EQUALS `s 12A an unsubstantiated representation in trade`
    AND NOT (    (   c's `provision engaged` EQUALS `s 9 misleading or deceptive conduct in trade`
                  OR c's `provision engaged` EQUALS `s 13 a false or misleading representation about goods or services`
                  OR c's `provision engaged` EQUALS `s 14(1) a false or misleading representation about land`)
             AND CONSIDER c's `clause contracting out`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                 WHEN JUST k THEN `the clause validly contracts out under s 5D` k)

§§ `Vendor bids (s 14A)`

-- s 14A "(2) The vendor ... makes a false or misleading representation with
-- respect to the price of the property if the vendor, or any agent ..., makes
-- a vendor bid ... (3) However, subsection (2) does not apply if— (a) there
-- is a reserve price for the property; and (b) the bid is made before the
-- reserve price is reached and is clearly identified as a vendor bid."
@ref s 14A
GIVEN v IS A `Vendor bid facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vendor bid is a false representation about price` v IF
    NOT (    v's `there is a reserve price`
         AND v's `the bid is below the reserve price`
         AND v's `the bid was identified as a vendor bid`)

§§ `Unsolicited goods (s 21A)`

-- s 21A "(1) ... the recipient— (a) is not liable— (i) to pay for the goods;
-- ... but (b) must, at any reasonable time during the period of 10 working
-- days after the day on which the recipient receives those goods, make those
-- goods available for collection ... (3) Subsection (4) applies if— (a) the
-- period referred to in subsection (1)(b) has expired; or (b) a sender has
-- failed to comply with subsection (2) ... (4) ... the recipient takes the
-- goods as an unconditional gift ... (5) However, subsection (4) does not
-- apply if the recipient— (a) has failed, without reasonable excuse, to
-- comply with subsection (1)(b); or (b) knew, or ought reasonably to have
-- known, that— (i) the goods were not intended for the recipient; or (ii) the
-- sender had no right to send".
@ref s 21A
GIVEN expired IS A BOOLEAN, `sender did not inform` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed to make available` IS A BOOLEAN, knew IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient takes the unsolicited goods as a gift, 10 working days passed:` expired `, a trader sender did not inform:` `sender did not inform` `, failed without excuse to make them available:` `failed to make available` `, knew they were not meant for them:` knew IF
        (expired OR `sender did not inform`)
    AND NOT `failed to make available`
    AND NOT knew

§§ `Specified trade contracts (ss 26C, 26D)`

-- s 26C(2) a small trade contract: "(a) each party to it is engaged in
-- trade; and (b) it is not a consumer contract; and (c) it does not comprise
-- or form part of a trading relationship that exceeds the annual value
-- threshold when the relationship first arises." s 26D(3)(b) the threshold
-- is exceeded if consideration "of at least the specified amount" is
-- provided for or more likely than not; (4) the specified amount is $250,000
-- (small trade) or $1 million (grocery supply).
@ref ss 26C(2), 26D
GIVEN `all in trade` IS A BOOLEAN, consumer IS A BOOLEAN, `annual value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a small trade contract, all parties in trade:` `all in trade` `, a consumer contract:` consumer `, annual value when the relationship arose` `annual value` IF
    `all in trade` AND (NOT consumer) AND `annual value` LESS THAN 250000

@ref ss 26C(3), 26D
GIVEN `all in trade` IS A BOOLEAN, consumer IS A BOOLEAN, `with a regulated grocery retailer` IS A BOOLEAN, `annual value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a grocery supply contract, all parties in trade:` `all in trade` `, a consumer contract:` consumer `, between a regulated grocery retailer and a supplier, for goods for consumers:` `with a regulated grocery retailer` `, annual value when the relationship arose` `annual value` IF
    `all in trade` AND (NOT consumer) AND `with a regulated grocery retailer` AND `annual value` LESS THAN 1000000

§§ `Unfair contract terms (ss 46I-46L)`

-- s 46K(1) "A court may not declare a term ... to be an unfair contract term
-- to the extent that the term— (a) defines the main subject matter of the
-- contract; or (b) sets the upfront price payable under the contract; or (c)
-- is a term required or expressly permitted by any enactment." s 46L(1) "A
-- term ... is unfair if the court is satisfied that the term— (a) would
-- cause a significant imbalance ...; and (b) is not reasonably necessary in
-- order to protect the legitimate interests of the party who would be
-- advantaged by the term; and (c) would cause detriment". (3) (b) is
-- presumed unless that party proves otherwise. s 46I(2) the contract is a
-- consumer contract or specified trade contract, and a standard form
-- contract (s 46J).
@ref ss 46I, 46J, 46K, 46L
@export Whether a court may declare a contract term unfair under ss 46I-46L of the Fair Trading Act 1986 (NZ): the term is in a consumer contract or specified trade contract that is a standard form contract; it does not define the main subject matter, set the upfront price, or follow from an enactment; and it would cause a significant imbalance, is not reasonably necessary to protect the advantaged party's legitimate interests (presumed unless that party proves otherwise), and would cause detriment. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN `consumer or specified trade contract` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the contract is a consumer contract or a specified trade contract (s 26C)
      `standard form` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the court determines it is a standard form contract (s 46J)
      `excluded by s 46K` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the term defines the main subject matter, sets the upfront price, or is required or expressly permitted by an enactment
      imbalance IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the term would cause a significant imbalance in the parties' rights and obligations
      `shown to be reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the advantaged party proved the term is reasonably necessary to protect its legitimate interests
      detriment IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the term would cause detriment if applied, enforced or relied on
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term may be declared unfair, consumer or specified trade contract:` `consumer or specified trade contract` `, standard form:` `standard form` `, excluded by s 46K:` `excluded by s 46K` `, significant imbalance:` imbalance `, shown to be reasonably necessary:` `shown to be reasonably necessary` `, detriment:` detriment IF
        `consumer or specified trade contract`
    AND `standard form`
    AND NOT `excluded by s 46K`
    AND imbalance
    AND NOT `shown to be reasonably necessary`
    AND detriment
